> Module Types

# Shared types

Types used by more than one module. No tax rule lives here. See
`catala/CONVENTIONS.md` for the naming and mapping conventions.

## Filing status

26 U.S.C. § 1(a) to (d) sets four rate schedules: married individuals filing
joint returns and surviving spouses (§ 1(a)), heads of households (§ 1(b)),
unmarried individuals (§ 1(c)) and married individuals filing separate returns
(§ 1(d)). Surviving spouse is defined in § 2(a) and head of household in § 2(b)
(`sources/statute/irc-1.html`, `sources/statute/irc-2.html`). Form 1040 for
2024 calls the § 2(a) status "Qualifying surviving spouse (QSS)"
(`sources/forms-instructions/f1040--2024.pdf` p 1).

Direct File: the writable fact `/filingStatus` (`filingStatus.xml`, fact
`/filingStatus`) takes one of the five options listed in `/filingStatusOptions`
(`filingStatus.xml` lines 5-50): `marriedFilingJointly`,
`marriedFilingSeparately`, `single`, `headOfHousehold`,
`qualifiedSurvivingSpouse`. The constructors below map one to one, in the
same order as the Form 1040 checkboxes.

```catala-metadata
## The filing status checked on Form 1040, page 1.
declaration enumeration FilingStatus:
  -- Single
  -- MarriedFilingJointly
  -- MarriedFilingSeparately
  -- HeadOfHousehold
  -- QualifyingSurvivingSpouse
```

## Filer role

Direct File keeps one or two filers in the `/filers` collection
(`filers.xml`, fact `/filers`), with `isPrimaryFiler` marking the first.
Per-filer items (W-2s, 1099s, HSA contributions) carry a `*/filer` reference
so MFJ amounts can be split per spouse (scope.md section 3.1). In Catala,
per-filer items carry a `FilerRole` field instead of a reference.

```catala-metadata
## Which of the (at most two) filers an item belongs to.
declaration enumeration FilerRole:
  -- PrimaryFiler
  -- SecondaryFiler
```

## State of residence (scope only)

Direct File only accepts filers from the states in `/scopedStateOptions`
(`constants.xml` lines 327-360). `MoreThanOne` and `NoneOfThese` are the two
knockout options in that list, and Louisiana is deliberately commented out.
This enum is the full list as re-read on 2026-10-31 (scope.md section 11,
item 11). Federal tax does not otherwise depend on the state; the knockout
rules that use it belong to the knockout issues, not here.

```catala-metadata
## Where the filer lived in the tax year, as Direct File asks it.
declaration enumeration ScopedState:
  -- MoreThanOne
  -- AK
  -- AZ
  -- CA
  -- CT
  -- FL
  -- ID
  -- IL
  -- KS
  -- ME
  -- MD
  -- MA
  -- NV
  -- NH
  -- NJ
  -- NM
  -- NY
  -- NC
  -- OR
  -- PA
  -- SD
  -- TN
  -- TX
  -- WA
  -- WI
  -- WY
  -- NoneOfThese
```
